{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792867515,"nonce":"E9f76G89Q8/Eru2lUd8Yn96BGic=","title":"OSR: a union built inside a loop is taken for a live-in, so an outlined region defines its parameter twice","message":"The OSR layout decides what a region defines with its own list of instruction kinds (instruction_result in osr.rs), which has no arm for CreateUnion, GetUnionDiscriminant or ExtractUnionValue; eefdcb18 let those instructions into layouts without adding them there. A union a loop body builds and reads (every generator pull loop does: the step decoded into Some/None and the item extracted) was therefore a live-in, and outline kept its id for the region's parameter while the body went on defining it: two definitions of one value. Optimisation then treats a cast of the item as reading the parameter and hoists it to the entry, so every pass boxes the stale value.\n\nSeen once generators yield typed lists: `list(gen())` twice in one function segfaulted in zb_list_to_any_i64 on a null list after the interpreted frame left for the outlined region (always with the default tiers; fine with ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1 or interpreter only). The layout now uses HirInstruction::result_id, which covers every kind.","files":null}]}